      "act": "MECHANISM",
      "role_note": "Transform: config upgrades mapped to engines; the LLM held to suggestions.",
      "narration_text": "Transform is where each upgrade meets an engine. Open Rewrite does the heavy lifting: Java seventeen, Jakarta, Hibernate, J-Unit. Each is a ready-made recipe that edits the syntax tree, so it changes only what it targets. Eclipse Transformer handles third-party jars. Descriptors get targeted X.M.L. rewrites, and the server config becomes J-Boss C.L.I. scripts. An L.L.M. may propose fixes for leftover errors, but only as suggestions you review.",
